CAT = "bcreContracts"; SEG = "CON"
Q = [
("A brokerage will list a client's home for sale. Unless the client waives it, what is needed before the brokerage represents the client in offering the home?",
 "A written service agreement", ["A verbal promise of exclusivity", "A sold-comparables report", "A signed offer from a buyer"],
 "Rule 43 requires a written service agreement, signed before the brokerage represents the seller in offering the real estate."),
("A listing service agreement for trading services must state:",
 "The date the agreement expires", ["The name of the seller's lawyer", "The closing date of the home sale", "The date the buyer's deposit is due"],
 "It must give the effective date and the expiry date, the services, remuneration and when it is payable, and personal information provisions."),
("A listing agreement is split between the listing brokerage and a cooperating brokerage. The agreement must show:",
 "What each brokerage will receive", ["The listing price history", "The cooperating agent's licence number", "The buyer's deposit method"],
 "It must state the remuneration the seller pays the listing brokerage, what the listing brokerage pays the cooperating brokerage and what it keeps."),
("A client and brokerage want to change a signed service agreement. The change must be:",
 "In writing and signed by both", ["Agreed by telephone only", "Noted in the brokerage's records", "Filed with the land title office"],
 "Any amendment of or addition to a required service agreement must be in writing and signed by the client and an authorized signatory of the brokerage."),
("A brokerage signs a written agreement with a client. The brokerage must give the client a copy:",
 "Immediately on signing", ["At the next showing of the home", "Within one year of signing", "Only on request by the client"],
 "Rule 44 requires immediate delivery of a copy of any written agreement for real estate services on its execution."),
("For a buyer's rescission of a residential contract, the prescribed period is:",
 "3 business days", ["24 hours", "7 calendar days", "30 calendar days"],
 "The Home Buyer Rescission Period Regulation sets the period at 3 business days after the date the acceptance of the offer was signed."),
("Which purchase is covered by the home buyer rescission right?",
 "A strata apartment", ["A home built on leased land", "A home sold at an auction", "A sale made under a court order"],
 "Covered property includes houses, townhouses and residential strata lots. Leased land, leasehold interests, auctions and court sales are exempt."),
("A buyer wants to rescind. A notice of rescission may be sent by:",
 "Email with a requested read receipt", ["A text message to the seller", "Ordinary mail to the seller's address", "A phone call to the seller's own agent"],
 "A notice is deemed served if sent by registered mail, by fax or by email with a requested read receipt, using the contact details in the contract."),
("Which detail must a notice of rescission include?",
 "The address or parcel identifier", ["The licensee's own licence number", "The lender's name and its address", "The number on the deposit receipt"],
 "A notice must contain the address, parcel identifier or a description of the property, the buyer's name and signature, each seller's name and the date."),
("Can a buyer sign away the right of rescission in the contract?",
 "No, it cannot be waived", ["Yes, if the seller asks", "Yes, if a lawyer is present", "Yes, for a lower price"],
 "The regulation says the right of rescission cannot be waived, so a waiver clause has no effect."),
("A buyer properly rescinds and a deposit was paid to the brokerage. After the seller's amount is taken, the rest of the deposit goes to:",
 "The buyer", ["The listing brokerage", "The seller", "The cooperating brokerage"],
 "The seller's amount is paid from the deposit and the remainder must be paid promptly to the buyer."),
("The rescission period is counted from after the date:",
 "The acceptance of the offer was signed", ["The last subject was removed by the buyer", "Possession was given to the buyer", "Title was registered at the office"],
 "Section 42 gives the buyer the prescribed number of days after the date the acceptance of the offer was signed."),
("Title to a house has already been transferred to the buyer. The buyer's right of rescission is:",
 "Gone, since title has transferred", ["Still open for another three days", "Open until the end of the month", "Extended by a further full week"],
 "Section 42 does not apply once title has been transferred from the seller to the buyer."),
("A contract respecting land is generally unenforceable unless:",
 "It is evidenced in a signed writing", ["It was witnessed by two people", "A lawyer drafted it for both sides", "It was notarized in person at once"],
 "Section 59 of the Law and Equity Act requires a signed writing, or acts such as part performance or reasonable reliance, to enforce a contract respecting land."),
("Under the Law and Equity Act, paying a deposit under a land contract may:",
 "Show that a contract was made", ["Void the contract at once", "Prove that the title is clear", "Replace the signed writing rule"],
 "Payment or acceptance of a deposit or part payment counts as an act indicating that a contract not inconsistent with the one alleged has been made."),
("Which element must appear prominently in all of a licensee's real estate advertising?",
 "The brokerage's licensee name", ["The licensee's own home address", "The history of the sale price", "The brokerage's years in business"],
 "Rule 40 requires the licensee name of the brokerage to be displayed prominently and in an easily readable way in all advertising."),
("May a licensee advertise a house as for sale before the owner has agreed to the advertising?",
 "No, the owner must consent first", ["Yes, if the listing is only verbal", "Yes, if the price is not stated", "Yes, if marked 'coming soon'"],
 "Rule 42 forbids advertising specific real estate as offered for sale unless the owner or the owner's authorized agent has consented."),
("A licensee's advertisement says a home has a new roof, which the licensee knows is false. This advertisement is:",
 "Prohibited as misleading", ["Fine if a buyer sees the home", "Fine if the price is fair", "Fine if only online"],
 "A licensee must not publish advertising that they know or reasonably ought to know contains a false or misleading statement."),
("Advertising by a member of a registered real estate team about trading services must show:",
 "The team's name", ["Each member's phone number", "The team's sales totals", "A list of past clients"],
 "Rule 40 requires advertising published by a team or by a team member regarding trading services to identify the team's name."),
("When must a group of licensees register as a real estate team?",
 "When they present themselves as one entity", ["When they share a brokerage's office space", "When they split commissions on some deals", "When they all work in the same city"],
 "Two or more licensees must register as a team with the superintendent if they hold themselves out as a single entity (other than a brokerage) or regularly work together as implied or designated agents of the same client."),
("A licensee promises a seller they will buy the home back later. Before making the promise the licensee must:",
 "Give a signed statement of details", ["Tell the seller about it verbally", "Get the managing broker's verbal approval", "Ask the buyer's lawyer to confirm it"],
 "Rule 49 bars inducement representations such as promises to resell or arrange financing unless a signed statement setting out all details is delivered at that time."),
("Which conduct is prohibited when a buyer and seller already have a signed contract?",
 "Persuading a party to break it", ["Reminding the buyer of a deadline", "Explaining the closing process", "Sending a copy to the lawyer"],
 "Rule 48 prohibits a licensee from inducing any party to an agreement for a trade in real estate to break it in order to enter into another agreement."),
("A licensee works from a home office that is not the brokerage office. The licensee may NOT:",
 "Put up an outdoor sign", ["Keep client files there", "Make phone calls there", "Meet clients there by appointment"],
 "Rule 37 bars signs indicating that services are provided from a personal office, answering its phone in the brokerage's name and showing its address in advertising."),
("A person who transfers land in fee simple must deliver to the transferee:",
 "A registrable transfer", ["A copy of the tax notice", "A survey of the neighbour's lot", "A letter from the strata council"],
 "Property Law Act s. 5 requires the transferor of fee simple land to deliver a transfer in registrable form under the Land Title Act."),
]
